cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these tools, please cite the Zenodo software record of Abyssal Claims Tools."
title: "Abyssal Claims Tools: browser-based checks of marine data files, metadata and licences"
abstract: >-
  Web tools that check marine datasets before they are published or reused.
  Data check reads data tables (CSV, TSV, Excel, PANGAEA, Darwin Core) and their
  metadata and reports problems with coordinates, positions on land, stations at
  inconsistent positions, dates, units, value ranges and licences, each explained
  in plain words with the source of every threshold. Licence check compares the
  licence that the metadata sources of one dataset state (Zenodo, PANGAEA,
  GeoNetwork, DataCite). Collection review reads the metadata of a whole
  collection and produces a fix list of missing, unclear or contradictory
  licences and empty metadata fields. Files dropped by a user are read in the
  user's browser and never leave it.
type: software
# `version`, `date-released` and the record's own `doi` are set at release time and must match the tag.
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
